#---
# purpose: a self-recursive call that hands an activation a list head outside the type its key names still has that head tested at runtime, so is_atom answers the same on all three paths
# oracle: self
# oracle.stamp: db9d73f4e6fb05fa
#---
#
# `walk/2` is entered with `[1]`, so its key says the head is an int. The
# recursive call passes `[:a | t]`, so the head can also be an atom. A key is
# an identity, not evidence: the head's type is what the activation's calls
# supply, and `is_atom(h)` must read the value rather than the key.
#
defmodule Main do
  def walk([h | t], n) do
    if n == 0 do
      is_atom(h)
    else
      walk([:a | t], n - 1)
    end
  end

  def main() do
    IO.inspect(walk([1], 2))
  end
end
Main.main()
